<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<Defs>

	<!--
		The soldier beetle's armament (2026-10-01, CASTES-PLAN.md phase 5). The mockup asks for "one
		of ripper blades, charger claw or megaspider horn", and all three are VRE Insector genes that
		already exist, so this def is the list and Source/Insects/BeetleArmament.cs is the pick - the
		same shape the castes' body colours use (HANDOFF.md §5.13): the register is XML, the code
		never names a weapon.

		Why a gene and not the race: CASTES-PLAN.md §0 decision 11 empties her race's tool list so
		the weapon gene owns the weapon, which is also the mantis's shape (HANDOFF.md §5.18). Nothing
		is lost by that - VRE's three weapon genes grant a hediff with a
		`HediffCompProperties_VerbGiver`, not a race tool, so she attacks with the same ripper-blades,
		claws or horn as any VRE insectoid.

		Why this gene is visible at all: a roll is invisible until it lands, so her xenotype lists the
		roll and her gene page shows what it gave her. One of the three appears beside this one.

		The cost sits on the weapon genes themselves - this wrapper is free of metabolic cost and
		charges one complexity point, so she is never billed twice for her armament. Out of the
		random gene sets for the same reason the quarrels are: a trader's genepack should not hand a
		stranger a beetle's weapon.

		Its icon is core's claw art for now - see the iconPath below - and hand art at
		Textures/UI/Icons/Genes/Gene_BeetleArmament replaces it when it exists.
	-->
	<GeneDef>
		<defName>PMM_Gene_BeetleArmament</defName>
		<label>beetle armament</label>
		<description>Her carapace grows one of three killing tools - a pair of ripper-blades, charger claws, or a megaspider horn - and which one is hers is settled when she is born.</description>
		<geneClass>PMM_Insects.Gene_BeetleArmament</geneClass>
		<!-- Core's claw art, borrowed while hers is undrawn: it is the closest thing in the family
		     to "a weapon grown out of her body", it is already loaded (PMM.Core is a dependency),
		     and she never carries the gene it belongs to, so nothing on her gene page repeats.
		     Hand art at Textures/UI/Icons/Genes/Gene_BeetleArmament replaces it when it exists. -->
		<iconPath>UI/Icons/Genes/PMM_Gene_MamonoClaws</iconPath>
		<displayCategory>Miscellaneous</displayCategory>
		<displayOrderInCategory>1005</displayOrderInCategory>
		<biostatMet>0</biostatMet>
		<biostatCpx>1</biostatCpx>
		<canGenerateInGeneSet>false</canGenerateInGeneSet>
		<modExtensions>
			<li Class="PMM_Insects.BeetleArmamentRoll">
				<armaments>
					<!-- The three the mockup names, in its order. They exclude each other's ground -
					     VRE_MegaspiderHorns excludes the Headbone cosmetic tag, the other two carry
					     their own lists - so the roll must be their only writer, and
					     BeetleArmament.Roll removes whichever one she already has before it adds
					     the new one. -->
					<li>VRE_RipperBlades</li>
					<li>VRE_ChargerClaws</li>
					<li>VRE_MegaspiderHorns</li>
				</armaments>
			</li>
		</modExtensions>
	</GeneDef>

</Defs>
